========================================================================
 Dusklight - Nintendo Switch build
 Open-source Twilight Princess reimplementation, GameCube -> Switch port
========================================================================

WHAT THIS IS
------------
A homebrew NRO that runs the Dusklight engine (TP reimplementation) on a
modded Switch via our own NVK (Vulkan) graphics stack. The NRO is
self-provisioning: it bundles a default config and a PRE-WARMED shader
cache, and writes them into its data folder on first boot, so installation
is basically just this one file (no/little texture & 3D-model pop-in).

REQUIREMENTS
------------
1. A Switch on CFW (Atmosphere) with a homebrew launcher (hbmenu) or Sphaira.
2. Your OWN legally-dumped Twilight Princess GameCube disc image (NOT
   included). US release (GZ2E01), ~1.46 GB. ANY format/name works:
   .gcm / .iso / .rvz / .ciso / .gcz / .wbfs - no need to rename it.

INSTALL - basically just the .nro
---------------------------------
1. Copy dusklight.nro to  sdmc:/switch/
2. Launch it once from hbmenu. It creates sdmc:/TwilitRealm/Dusklight/ and
   writes the pre-warmed shader cache there automatically.
3. Put your TP dump (any name/format) into sdmc:/TwilitRealm/Dusklight/
4. Launch again - Dusklight auto-detects the disc and runs.

No manual folder layout, no data_location.json, no game/ folder. Everything
the app reads/writes lives under sdmc:/TwilitRealm/Dusklight/ (the only
exceptions are this .nro in sdmc:/switch/ and CFW crash reports in
sdmc:/atmosphere/).

WHAT WORKS
----------
- Audio (JAudio2/DSP -> libnx audren).
- Gyro on by default (bow/slingshot/clawshot aiming + look mode); tune or
  disable in Settings -> Gyro.
- In-game menu: press MINUS (-) during gameplay.
- Automatic disc detection in the data folder (any name/format).
- Pipeline-compilation notification + achievement toasts.
- Changing Internal Resolution / aspect ratio (4:3) no longer crashes.
- Pre-warmed shader cache -> little/no first-run pop-in.

NOTES
-----
- Launcher/menus run at 60fps. In-game is ~30fps (TP's native GameCube rate).
  Frame interpolation is present but not yet producing extra frames (WIP).
- Per-file self-heal: on boot the NRO restores ANY missing seed file from its
  bundled copy - config.json, dawn_cache.db or pipeline_cache.db - one by one
  (the folder need not be empty). Files you already have are never overwritten.
- The cache is read-write: missing shaders compile once and persist. Deleting
  the .db files just recompiles on demand (and the seed is restored next boot).
- Saves use the GameCube memory-card format (.gci) under .../USA/. An older
  save from sdmc:/aurora/ is auto-imported on first boot.

